  "verified_mechanisms": [
    "Rust lays out the four header controls in the existing 134-point strip, with 32-point controls and 2-point gaps. Native outer titlebar placement, traffic-light region and empty-header dragging remain adapters.",
    "Main-window controls use the established Rust pointer/key reducer and existing Chromium page-command callbacks. Native button names, disabled state, focus and default accessibility actions remain.",
    "Rust emits back/forward/reload shape IDs and sidebar/hover/focus primitives. Metal evaluates analytic line/arc signed distances for navigation icons using the existing 32-byte quad ABI; no third-party icon/font asset was added.",
    "The main window and sidebar are separate native windows. Each has its own small opaque Metal canvas, while both surfaces share the same device, command queue and pipeline through a weak context cache. Strong GPU ownership ends with the last surface.",
    "Header invalidations coalesce independently before native rasterization. The canvas uses native visible bounds so the top titlebar clip is preserved, refreshes on native window movement/theme/visibility and remains active while the sidebar is hidden.",
    "The sidebar-toggle glyph reflects actual sidebar visibility. Unchanged selected values no longer schedule repeated paints. Identical scene fingerprints skip GPU submission, and no idle rendering timer is introduced.",
    "Scene glyph painting skips native children as well as icon content while Metal is visible, preventing a native focus-ring record from painting over scene-owned focus. Native fallback is restored when Metal becomes unavailable.",
    "The new native regression clicks disabled Forward without changing history, physically navigates Back/Forward, reloads a real document and checks a JavaScript marker is cleared. It also toggles the sidebar, moves the window, verifies focus paint routing and hides/restores the main window.",
    "The full prior sidebar, footer, vertical/horizontal scroll, split/folder/pin/session, workspace transition, settings, keyboard and large-sidebar matrix remains green."
  ],
  "manual_observations": [
    "The matching signed and timestamped app showed the new back/forward/reload icons alongside the native traffic-light/profile region without obscuring the original split pair.",
    "Opening a loopback page enabled Back. Clicking Back restored the original URL/title and enabled Forward; Forward returned to the test page.",
    "Hiding the sidebar left the header visible and usable. Changing the page title in JavaScript and clicking Reload restored the URL-defined title, demonstrating actual reload with the sidebar hidden.",
    "Back restored the original page and split pair. The sidebar was shown and repinned, restoring the original demo mode. The prototype was closed and its launcher exited successfully.",
    "The normal application/profile was not used."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native outer frame/header placement, Button/View event and AX nodes, window drag hit testing, services and browser commands remain adapters. This is not complete Views container removal.",
    "Split pane headers/divider, resize/autohide state, native animation snapshots and remaining palettes/forms/services presentation still require migration.",
    "The new header case tests the active regular page. Existing peek targeting remains in the unchanged application command implementation but is not independently covered by that case.",
    "A full keyboard/VoiceOver/trackpad/RTL/scale matrix and controlled real-workload CPU/GPU/physical-presentation comparison remain required. Test durations and submitted frame counts are not presentation measurements.",
    "No new third-party binary dependency was introduced; original-code Apache-2.0 and required upstream notices are unchanged."
  ]
